# Key Simulation

This extension simulates key presses and mouse clicks directly in the Scratch VM. It is useful for re-keybinding, custom control schemes, mobile support, and automated testing.

Events are only sent to the Scratch VM. This extension does **not** type text into editor fields and it does not click editor buttons.

<hr>

<h3 id="press_key">Press Key Block <span class="heading-link">(<a href="#press_key">#</a>)</span></h3>

```scratch
press [space v] for (0.1) seconds and wait? :: #BF0000
```

Presses the chosen keyboard key, keeps it held for the given number of seconds, then releases it. This can be used to trigger the built-in <code class="inline">key (space v) pressed?</code> boolean and <code class="inline">when (space v) key pressed</code> hat blocks.

Setting the duration to `0` presses the key for exactly one frame.

When the <code class="inline">and wait</code> option is enabled the block waits for the full duration before the next block runs. When it is disabled the key is pressed in the background and the next block runs immediately.

#### Example

```scratch
when green flag clicked
forever
  if <key (a v) pressed?> then
    press [up arrow v] for (0.1) seconds and wait? :: #BF0000
  end
end
```

This re-maps the <code class="inline">a</code> key to the up arrow key.

<hr>

<h3 id="hold_mouse">Hold Mouse Button Block <span class="heading-link">(<a href="#hold_mouse">#</a>)</span></h3>

```scratch
hold [left v] mouse button at x: (0) y: (0) for (0.1) seconds :: #BF0000
```

